## 4. Five direct quotations or data points a strategist must address

1. **NFPA 72 already sets the intelligibility floor.** "The voice intelligibility of an emergency communication system is considered acceptable if at least 90 percent of the measurement locations within each acoustically distinguishable space (ADS) have a measured STI of not less than 0.45 (0.65 CIS) and an average STI of not less than 0.50 (0.70 CIS)." [Source: https://www.commercialintegrator.com/security/mass_notification/mass-notification-intelligibility/] The strategist must explain why an MWAA standard adds safety above NFPA 72, and whether it adds legal exposure.

2. **The DCA political envelope is real and current.** The NTSB found the January 29, 2025 collision "resulted primarily from the placement of a helicopter route in close proximity to a runway approach path without procedural mitigations, combined with failures by multiple organizations to identify and address known risks," and issued 50 safety recommendations [Source: https://enotrans.org/article/ntsb-unveils-findings-probable-cause-and-recommendations-from-dca-mid-air-collision-investigation/]. The strategist must explain how a quiet-by-design standard survives a post-incident hearing in which MWAA is asked to defend audible-information reductions at DCA.

3. **Silent airports produce documented passenger harm.** European Consumer Centre Austria, official advisory: **"the airport is not obliged to make announcements via speakers in order to guarantee that every single passenger receives the information relevant to him. This means that if you are late at the gate and miss your flight or are denied boarding, you can't blame the airport for not knowing your gate or if you waited to be called out"** [Source: https://europakonsument.at/en/page/tips-silent-airports]. The strategist must explain what MWAA's answer is to the passenger who misses a flight because the airport chose not to page.

4. **Getting the acoustic-architectural coordination wrong is expensive.** Documented terminal case: **"USD $2.8 million in remediation, eight weeks of disruption, and immeasurable passenger frustration. The acoustic consultant's prediction of STI 0.38 was documented but overruled by architectural vision"** [Source: https://acousplan.com/blog/iec-60268-16-sti-measurement]. The strategist must show that MWAA's standard would have prevented this failure, and at what cost to the program schedule.

5. **The 15-year U&L closed the airline lever.** The 2025 U&L took effect 1 January 2025 and runs through 2039, alongside a $9.0B joint capital plan [context packet §3]. Airline gate announcements are the loudest recurring PA source. The strategist must show a credible path by which airline gate-agent behavior changes without the U&L amendment airlines have no incentive to sign.

